# .gitignore for the GENERATED PROJECT (not the template repo itself).
#
# Replace the generated project's root .gitignore with this file as part of
# the first scaffold step. Two purposes:
#
#  1. Standard ignores for Java/Node build output and IDE files.
#  2. **Exclude the template-only control plane** so that when the user does
#     `git init` + `git remote add origin <company-repo>` + `git push`, the
#     canonical scaffolds and embedded source documents do not pollute the
#     company repository.
#
#     The active dual-agent runtime is part of the app: AGENTS.md, replit.md,
#     .agents/, CLAUDE.md, and .claude/ are committed so both agents work after
#     clone. Engineering handoff removes only the Replit surface explicitly.

# ====================================================================
# Template-only control plane — DO NOT COMMIT TO COMPANY REPO
# ====================================================================
# Canonical sources are absent from a materialized project and never belong in
# its Git history. Both active agent surfaces are deliberately NOT ignored.
templates/
custom_instruction/
# Note: .replit and replit.nix DO get committed — they're part of the runnable
# app (define how Replit launches it). Only the rule-set files are excluded.

# ====================================================================
# Replit auto-injected Python files — never wanted in a Java/React app
# ====================================================================
# Replit's default workspace bootstrap drops Python scaffolding even when
# the user picks a Java template. Delete + gitignore so it can't leak.
main.py
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
poetry.lock
requirements.txt
Pipfile
Pipfile.lock
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# ====================================================================
# Secrets / env
# ====================================================================
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*service-account*.json
*credentials*.json

# ====================================================================
# IDE / OS
# ====================================================================
.idea/
# Shared Claude rules/docs/skills are part of the engineering contract and are
# committed. Only personal settings, installation state, and per-task working
# artifacts stay local.
.claude/agents/
.claude/commands/
.claude/gsd-core/
.claude/hooks/
.claude/scripts/
.claude/.gsd-profile
.claude/gsd-file-manifest.json
.claude/package.json
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/gsd-install-state.json
.claude/tasks/*
!.claude/tasks/README.md
*.iml
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# ====================================================================
# Java / Maven
# ====================================================================
target/
*.class
*.jar
*.war
*.ear
hs_err_pid*
.mvn/timing.properties
.mvn/wrapper/maven-wrapper.jar

# ====================================================================
# Node / frontend
# ====================================================================
node_modules/
dist/
.cache/
*.tsbuildinfo
backend/application/src/main/resources/static/

# ====================================================================
# Generated sources (OpenAPI codegen, etc.)
# ====================================================================
generated-sources/
generated/
frontend/src/shared/api/generated/*
!frontend/src/shared/api/generated/.gitkeep

# ====================================================================
# Replit workspace local state
# ====================================================================
.config/
.local/
.upm/
.cache/
.breakpoints
.replit.local

# ====================================================================
# Replit Agent's Node/Express bias — empty server/ at project root
# ====================================================================
# Replit Agent's default for "server" mode is a Node/Express scaffold
# that lives at `server/`. This template forbids Node backends; if
# the directory shows up empty after generation, it's an artifact —
# delete and keep ignored so Agent doesn't repopulate it.
server/
